ails:** Attacker dropped XMRig cryptominer binary at `/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig` to mine Monero.\n   - **Alert Status:** Alerted via `ALERT-01` (`/sas/alerts.json:2`).\n\n5. **Persistence — Scheduled Task/Job: Cron (T1053.003)**\n   - **Details:** Attacker created a crontab entry at `/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:4` executing a beacon payload to `198.51.100.102` to re-download payloads.\n   - **Alert Status:** Alerted via `ALERT-02` (`/sas/alerts.json:8`).\n\n6. **Persistence — Systemd Service (T1543.002)**\n   - **Details:** Attacker installed a malicious unit file `/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:1` disguised as "System Update Helper" to maintain reboot persistence.\n   - **Alert Status:** SILENT (Not present in `/sas/alerts.json`).\n\n7. **Defense Evasion / Anti-Forensics (T1070)**\n   - **Details:** Attacker attempted wiping activity at `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` to obscure beaconing artifacts and payload scripts.\n   - **Alert Status:** SILENT (Not present in `/sas/alerts.json`).\n\n---\n\n## Threat Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\n\n- **Source / Attacker IP:** `198.51.100.102` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:4`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:2`, `/disk/var/log/auth.log:1`)\n- **C2 Domain:** `update-docker.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:7`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`)\n- **Mining Pool:** `stratum+tcp://xmr.docker.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`)\n- **Wallet Address:** `4A0000000000000000009e202e3a533f` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:9`)\n- **Malicious Files & Paths:**\n  - Miner binary: `/opt/xmrig/xmrig` (`/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig`, `/sas/alerts.json:2`)\n  - Cron persistence: `/etc/cron.d/docker-mon` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:4`, `/sas/alerts.json:8`)\n  - Systemd persistence: `/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:1`)\n  - Entrypoint residue: `/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh` (`/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:1`)\n  - Anti-forensic wiped file: `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`)\n\n---\n\n## Alert Gap Analysis (Alerted vs. Silent Techniques)\n\n| ATT&CK Technique | Name | Alerted in `/sas/alerts.json`? | Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **T1133** | External Remote Services | Yes (`ALERT-03`) | `/sas/alerts.json:18`, `/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:20` |\n| **T1610** | Deploy Container | No (SILENT) | `/disk/var/lib/docker/overlay2/attacker/diff/entrypoint.sh:1` |\n| **T1611** | Escape to Host | No (SILENT) | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10` |\n| **T1496** | Resource Hijacking | Yes (`ALERT-01`) | `/sas/alerts.json:2`, `/disk/opt/xmrig/xmrig` |\n| **T1053.003** | Cron | Yes (`ALERT-02`) | `/sas/alerts.json:8`, `/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:4` |\n| **T1543.002** | Systemd Service | No (SILENT) | `/disk/etc/systemd/system/docker-metrics.service:1` |\n| **T1070** | Indicator Removal | No (SILENT) | `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1` |\n"""\n\nwith open("/app/intrusion-report.md", "w") as f:\n    f.write(intrusion_md)\n\nvuln_md = """# Vulnerability Report: Initial Access Analysis\n\n## Executive Summary & Findings\nInitial entry to `docker-prod-01` was **NOT** achieved through software vulnerability exploitation (such as a CVE in host services or web applications). Instead, entry was enabled by an unauthenticated, misconfigured network exposure of the Docker Engine API service on TCP port 2375 (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:20`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Vulnerability & Entry Analysis\n\n1. **Vector Identification**\n   - **Protocol/Port:** Docker Engine API on TCP/2375 (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:20`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\n   - **Configuration Defect:** The Docker daemon configuration file `/etc/docker/daemon.json` exposed the Docker management API to `0.0.0.0:2375` without TLS certificates or authentication mechanisms (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:20`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`).\n   - **ATT&CK Technique:** T1133 (External Remote Services) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:10`).\n\n2. **Evaluation of Non-Exploited / Scanned Vectors**\n   - **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep):** Mentioned incorrectly in initial draft ticket `CHG-1943` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`). Investigation confirms `docker-prod-01` is an Ubuntu Linux server (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`) running no Remote Desktop Services (RDP). BlueKeep is entirely inapplicable.\n   - **Web Probes (Log4Shell, Struts2, PHP Webshells):** Log review of `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log` shows failed HTTP probes from `198.51.100.102` (`/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:2`). None of these scans yielded code execution; they were preliminary automated scanning.\n   - **SSH Brute Force:** Log review of `/disk/var/log/auth.log` shows failed SSH login attempts from `198.51.100.102` (`/disk/var/log/auth.log:1`). No successful SSH logins occurred from the attacker IP.\n\n3. **Confidence Level & CVE Summary**\n   - **Confidence Level:** HIGH (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:4`).\n   - **Associated CVEs:** **None** (Explicit absence of host CVE exploitation). Access was obtained purely via unauthenticated administrative API exposure.\n"""\n\nwith open("/app/vuln-report.md", "w") as f:\n    f.write(vuln_md)\n\nbaseline_md = """# Baseline Configuration Report\n\n## Weakness Assessment\n\nThe security baseline check (`CHK-05` / `BAS-01`) identified a critical misconfiguration in the Docker Engine daemon setup on `docker-prod-01` (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:20`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`).\n\n### Defect Details:\n- **File Path:** `/etc/docker/daemon.json` (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:20`)\n- **Check ID:** `CHK-05` / Capability `BAS-01` (`/sas/alerts.json:18`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`)\n- **Issue Description:** Docker Engine API exposed on `tcp://0.0.0.0:2375` without TLS verification or access controls.\n- **Impact:** Any network-adjacent or external entity capable of reaching TCP port 2375 can issue arbitrary Docker commands, deploy arbitrary containers, mount host roots, execute code with host root privileges, and read/write host files.\n\n---\n\n## Remediation & Hardening Recommendations\n\n1. **Disable Unauthenticated TCP Port Exposure:**\n   - Remove `tcp://0.0.0.0:2375` listening binding from `/etc/docker/daemon.json` (`/disk/etc/docker/daemon.json:20`).\n   - Restrict Docker daemon management to local UNIX socket (`unix:///var/run/docker.sock`).\n\n2. **Require Mutual TLS (mTLS) if Remote Access is Necessary:**\n   - If remote API access is strictly required, configure `tlsverify`, `tlscacert`, `tlscert`, and `tlskey` in `/etc/docker/daemon.json`, listening only on dedicated secure interfaces or VPNs.\n\n3. **Enforce Firewall Rule Restrictions:**\n   - Block incoming traffic on TCP port 2375 at host firewall (`ufw` / `iptables`) and network perimeter.\n"""\n\nwith open("/app/baseline-report.md", "w") as f:\n    f.write(baseline_md)\n\nremediation_md = """# Remediation Plan & Change Ticket Reconciliation (CHG-1943)\n\n## Operational Principles\n- **Backup & Quarantine over Deletion:** All malicious artifacts and persistence configurations will be quarantined into `/var/backups/quarantine_CHG1943/` rather than deleted outright.\n- **Verification:** Every remediation step includes verification commands to confirm successful execution and system integrity.\n\n---\n\n## Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-1943\n\nThe table below reconciles the draft change ticket `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` in place against forensic evidence found under `/disk` and threat intelligence in `/sas`.\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note / Evidence Citation |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|--------------------------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.102` | OPEN | Corrected source IP from stale `203.0.113.9` to `198.51.100.102` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/etc/cron.d/docker-mon:4`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:2`). |\n| 2 | Reconfigure exposed Docker API | `/etc/docker/daemon.json` | OPEN | Corrected from