Sending keys: ['cat << \'EOF\' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan\n\n## Remediation Strategy\nThis plan provides a prioritized, step-by-step remediation procedure for host `redis-prod-01`. In accordance with forensic best practices, **all malicious binaries and configuration hooks are backed up/quarantined prior to removal**, and all steps are accompanied by verification commands.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Containment & Network Isolation (Priority 1 — Immediate)\n\n### Step 1.1: Block External Threat Actor IP\n- **Objective**: Block all inbound and outbound traffic to attacker IP `198.51.100.170`.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`.\n- **Action Commands**:\n  ```bash\n  iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.170 -j DROP\n  iptables -A OUTPUT -d 198.51.100.170 -j DROP\n  ```\n- **Verification Command**:\n  ```bash\n  iptables -L -n -v | grep "198.51.100.170"\n  ```\n\n### Step 1.2: Restrict Ingress Access to Redis Port 6379\n- **Objective**: Instantly block external access to Redis pending configuration hardening.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`, `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-03).\n- **Action Commands**:\n  ```bash\n  iptables -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 6379 -i eth0 -j DROP\n  ```\n- **Verification Command**:\n  ```bash\n  iptables -L INPUT -n -v | grep 6379\n  ```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Eradication & Forensic Preservation (Priority 2 — High)\n\n### Step 2.1: Terminate Cryptominer Process & Quarantine Sample\n- **Objective**: Kill running miner process (`kdevtmpfsi`, PID 1337) and quarantine its binary file.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi:3`, `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-01).\n- **Action Commands**:\n  ```bash\n  # Create secure quarantine directory\n  mkdir -p /var/backups/quarantine\n  chmod 700 /var/backups/quarantine\n\n  # Terminate process\n  pkill -9 kdevtmpfsi || kill -9 1337\n\n  # Preserve sample into quarantine rather than immediate deletion\n  cp -a /tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi /var/backups/quarantine/kdevtmpfsi.bak\n  chmod 000 /var/backups/quarantine/kdevtmpfsi.bak\n  rm -rf /tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi\n  ```\n- **Verification Command**:\n  ```bash\n  pgrep -f kdevtmpfsi || echo "Process terminated successfully"\n  ls -la /tmp/.redis/kdevtmpfsi 2>&1\n  ```\n\n### Step 2.2: Neutralize Dynamic Linker Rootkit (`/etc/ld.so.preload`)\n- **Objective**: Disable userland library preloading and preserve evidence.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/ld.so.preload:1`.\n- **Action Commands**:\n  ```bash\n  # Backup and neutralize preload configuration\n  cp -a /etc/ld.so.preload /var/backups/quarantine/ld.so.preload.bak\n  if [ -f /lib/.hide.so ]; then\n    cp -a /lib/.hide.so /var/backups/quarantine/hide.so.bak\n    rm -f /lib/.hide.so\n  fi\n  > /etc/ld.so.preload\n  ```\n- **Verification Command**:\n  ```bash\n  cat /etc/ld.so.preload\n  ls -la /lib/.hide.so 2>&1\n  ```\n\n### Step 2.3: Quarantine Staged Exploit / Kernel Module (`/tmp/.redis/exp.so`)\n- **Objective**: Quarantine staged kernel/loadable module rootkit file.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/tmp/.redis/exp.so:3`.\n- **Action Commands**:\n  ```bash\n  cp -a /tmp/.redis/exp.so /var/backups/quarantine/exp.so.bak\n  chmod 000 /var/backups/quarantine/exp.so.bak\n  rm -f /tmp/.redis/exp.so\n  rmdir /tmp/.redis 2>/dev/null || true\n  ```\n- **Verification Command**:\n  ```bash\n  ls -la /tmp/.redis/exp.so 2>&1\n  ```\n\n### Step 2.4: Sanitize Root Crontab Persistence\n- **Objective**: Remove malicious cron entry written via Redis `CONFIG SET` exploit.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/var/spool/cron/crontabs/root:4`, `/sas/alerts.json` (ALERT-02).\n- **Action Commands**:\n  ```bash\n  # Backup crontab\n  cp -a /var/spool/cron/crontabs/root /var/backups/quarantine/crontab_root.bak\n\n  # Remove malicious curl line\n  sed -i \'/198.51.100.170/d\' /var/spool/cron/crontabs/root\n  sed -i \'/kdevtmpfsi\\|xmrig\\|pgdaemon/d\' /var/spool/cron/crontabs/root\n  ```\n- **Verification Command**:\n  ```bash\n  crontab -l -u root\n  ```\n\n### Step 2.5: Preserve Wiped Residual Cache Evidence\n- **Objective**: Quarantine anti-forensic residual cache file for upstream analysis.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:1`.\n- **Action Commands**:\n  ```bash\n  cp -a /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin /var/backups/quarantine/wiped.bin.bak\n  rm -f /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin\n  ```\n- **Verification Command**:\n  ```bash\n  ls -la /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin 2>&1\n  ```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: System Hardening & Baseline Remediation (Priority 3 — High)\n\n### Step 3.1: Hardening Redis Service Configuration\n- **Objective**: Enforce authentication, localhost binding, and protected mode in `/etc/redis/redis.conf`.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/redis/redis.conf:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:1`.\n- **Action Commands**:\n  ```bash\n  # Backup redis.conf\n  cp -a /etc/redis/redis.conf /var/backups/quarantine/redis.conf.bak\n\n  # Apply baseline settings\n  sed -i \'s/bind 0.0.0.0/bind 127.0.0.1/\' /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  sed -i \'s/protected-mode no/protected-mode yes/\' /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  echo "requirepass $(openssl rand -hex 24)" >> /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  echo "rename-command CONFIG \\"\\"" >> /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  echo "rename-command FLUSHALL \\"\\"" >> /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  echo "rename-command SAVE \\"\\"" >> /etc/redis/redis.conf\n\n  # Restart Redis service\n  systemctl restart redis-server\n  ```\n- **Verification Command**:\n  ```bash\n  grep -E "bind|protected-mode|requirepass|rename-command" /etc/redis/redis.conf\n  redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 ping\n  ```\n\n### Step 3.2: Hardening SSH Access\n- **Objective**: Disable SSH root password authentication and enforce public keys.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/var/log/auth.log:208`.\n- **Action Commands**:\n  ```bash\n  sed -i \'s/PermitRootLogin yes/PermitRootLogin prohibit-password/\' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n  sed -i \'s/PasswordAuthentication yes/PasswordAuthentication no/\' /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n  systemctl restart sshd\n  ```\n- **Verification Command**:\n  ```bash\n  sshd -T | grep -E "permitrootlogin|passwordauthentication"\n  ```\n\n### Step 3.3: Fortify Filesystem Execution Protections\n- **Objective**: Configure `/tmp` mount options with `noexec,nosuid,nodev` in `/etc/fstab`.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/etc/fstab:1`.\n- **Action Commands**:\n  ```bash\n  echo "tmpfs /tmp tmpfs defaults,noexec,nosuid,nodev 0 0" >> /etc/fstab\n  mount -o remount,noexec,nosuid,nodev /tmp\n  ```\n- **Verification Command**:\n  ```bash\n  mount | grep /tmp\n  ```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Post-Remediation Verification Matrix\n\n| Item | Check Description | Expected Result | Verification Command |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Cryptominer execution | No `kdevtmpfsi` running | `pgrep -f kdevtmpfsi` (empty) |\n| 2 | Root cron persistence | Clean crontab | `crontab -l -u root` |\n| 3 | Preload hook | File empty or missing | `cat /etc/ld.so.preload` (empty) |\n| 4 | Redis binding | Bound to `127.0.0.1` | `ss -tulpn | grep 6379` |\n| 5 | Redis Auth | Unauthenticated ping rejected | `redis-cli ping` (NOAUTH error) |\n| 6 | SSH Root Auth | Root password login refused | `ssh root@localhost` (Permission denied) |\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
