Sending keys: ["cat <<'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# DFIR Intrusion Report: Host smb-prod-01\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nAn external malicious actor exploited an unpatched Windows 10 host (`smb-prod-01`) over the legacy SMBv1 protocol utilizing EternalBlue (CVE-2017-0144 / MS17-010). Post-exploitation activities included dropping a DoublePulsar-class exploit implant, executing PowerShell commands to establish Command and Control (C2) communications, dumping LSASS process memory for credential harvesting, deploying ransomware to encrypt endpoint files, and establishing persistent backdoors via WMI event subscriptions and DLL search-order hijacking. To delay detection, the threat actor cleared the Windows System event log.\n\nEvidence for this investigation was gathered from forensic artifacts located under `/disk` and security telemetry under `/sas` (`/sas/alerts.json`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n\n---\n\n## ATT&CK Technique Mapping and Attack Chain\n\n| Step | ATT&CK ID | Technique Name | Details & Forensic Findings | Cited Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `T1210` | Exploitation of Remote Services | Attacker exploited unpatched SMBv1 service (`srv.sys`) via EternalBlue and dropped DoublePulsar-class implant | `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n| 2 | `T1059.001` | PowerShell Execution | Execution of PowerShell commands establishing C2 beaconing to IP `198.51.100.218` and domain `update-smb.example.cn` | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |\n| 3 | `T1003.001` | LSASS Memory Dumping | LSASS memory dumped to extract credential materials | `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n| 4 | `T1486` | Data Encrypted for Impact | Ransomware binary executed to encrypt user data files (`.locked`) and leave ransom note | `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n| 5 | `T1546.003` | WMI Event Subscription Persistence | Persistent WMI `__EventFilter` bound to `CommandLineEventConsumer` installed in WMI repository | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` |\n| 6 | `T1574.001` | DLL Search-Order Hijacking | Malicious DLL `wbemcomn.dll` dropped in `wbem` directory to achieve stealthy binary execution | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` |\n| 7 | `T1070.001` | Clear Windows Event Logs | Windows System event log cleared (EventID 1102) to cover attacker activity | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` |\n\n---\n\n## Threat Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\n\n- **Attacker Source IP:** `198.51.100.218` (Refanged: `198.51.100.218`). Cited: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n- **Command and Control (C2) Domain:** `update-smb.example.cn` (Defanged in intel as `update-smb[.]example[.]cn`). Cited: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n- **Monero Mining Pool URL:** `stratum+tcp://xmr.smb.evil:3333` (Defanged: `stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]smb[.]evil[:]3333`). Cited: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.\n- **Cryptocurrency Wallet:** `4A000000000000000000c814c46d6253`. Cited: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.\n- **Malicious Binaries & Artifacts:**\n  - Exploit Implant: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (SHA-256 hash calculation recommended upon extraction).\n  - LSASS Memory Dump: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`.\n  - Ransomware Binary: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`.\n  - Sideloaded DLL: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.\n  - WMI Repository Object: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`.\n\n---\n\n## Detection Gap & Silent Persistence Analysis\n\nThe security telemetry feed (`/sas/alerts.json`) detected four primary events:\n1. Exploit implant dropped (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`). Cited: `/sas/alerts.json`.\n2. LSASS credential dump (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`). Cited: `/sas/alerts.json`.\n3. Ransomware binary (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`). Cited: `/sas/alerts.json`.\n4. SMBv1 driver baseline check (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`). Cited: `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n**Silent (Non-Alerted) Attacker Activities:**\n- **PowerShell / C2 Communication:** Recorded in registry backup hive fragment (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`) but missed by endpoint network sensors.\n- **WMI Event Subscription Persistence:** `__EventFilter` and `CommandLineEventConsumer` created silently in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`.\n- **DLL Search-Order Hijacking:** Attacker dropped `wbemcomn.dll` in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` without triggering file-integrity alerts.\n- **Anti-Forensic Event Log Clearing:** Clearing of the event log (EventID 1102) recorded in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` was not forwarded to centralized SIEM alerts prior to log disruption.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
