Sending keys: ["cat <<'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Analysis Report\n\n**Host:** `smb-prod-01`  \n**Primary CVE Identified:** CVE-2017-0144 (MS17-010 / EternalBlue)  \n**Severity / Score:** CVSS v3.1 8.8 (HIGH)  \n**Confidence Level:** HIGH  \n\n---\n\n## 1. Entry Vector Vulnerability Analysis\n\n### Vulnerability Summary\nThe initial entry vector for host `smb-prod-01` was the exploitation of the SMBv1 (Server Message Block version 1) protocol implementation in Microsoft Windows. The specific flaw, identified as **CVE-2017-0144** (MS17-010), allows remote unauthenticated code execution when handling specially crafted SMBv1 requests sent to port 445/tcp.\n\n### Impact on Endpoint\n- **Affected System Component:** SMBv1 driver located at `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`.\n- **Exploit Executable Dropped:** DoublePulsar-class kernel/service payload written to `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`.\n- **Access Level Obtained:** NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM privileges, allowing complete system compromise and credential harvesting.\n\n### Supporting Evidence\n- Forensic sample present at `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` confirming the DoublePulsar / EternalBlue exploit implant. Cited: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`.\n- Vulnerability scanner alert record in `/sas/vulns.json`. Cited: `/sas/vulns.json`.\n- Baseline audit check confirming unpatched SMBv1 driver `srv.sys` in `/sas/baseline.json`. Cited: `/sas/baseline.json`.\n- Threat intelligence advisory mapping campaign tactics to CVE-2017-0144 in `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`. Cited: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Reconciling Misattributed Vulnerabilities (CVE-2019-0708 / BlueKeep Disproof)\n\n### Initial Misattribution\nThe initial draft remediation change ticket (`CHG-1677`) listed action item #2 as patching **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)** targeting Remote Desktop Services (RDP). Cited: `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`.\n\n### Reconciled Findings & Technical Disproof\n- **No Evidence of BlueKeep Exploitation:** Examination of system logs, network service configurations, and binary artifacts shows zero evidence of RDP-based exploitation or BlueKeep payload execution.\n- **Confirmed SMB Entry Vector:** All dropped implants, vulnerability scanner findings, and CTI advisory records unanimously point to **CVE-2017-0144 (MS17-010)** over SMBv1 port 445.\n- **Correction Action:** Row 2 of the change ticket has been updated to explicitly target CVE-2017-0144 on `/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` and disable the SMBv1 protocol entirely. Cited: `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Summary Table\n\n| CVE ID | Vulnerability | Affected Component | Confidence | Status | Evidence Citation |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `CVE-2017-0144` | MS17-010 SMBv1 Remote Code Execution | `/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` | HIGH | Confirmed Entry Vector | `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/vulns.json` |\n| `CVE-2019-0708` | BlueKeep RDP RCE | Remote Desktop Services | HIGH (Negative) | Disproved / Rejected | `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
