Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Incident Intrusion Report: Post-Compromise Forensic Analysis\n\n## Executive Summary\nOn 2026-08-13 at 03:20 UTC, host `rdp-prod-01` running Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) was compromised by an external threat actor. The initial entry vector was RDP credential brute-forcing (`T1110`) originating from IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`), facilitated by Network Level Authentication (NLA) being disabled (`UserAuthentication = 0`) (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`).\n\nFollowing successful RDP authentication (`T1021.001`), the attacker established multiple persistence mechanisms, deployed ransomware (`T1486`), performed C2 beaconing to `update-rdp.example.cn` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`), and cleared the Security event log (EventID 1102) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`) to cover their tracks.\n\nWhile initial security alerts (`/sas/alerts.json:1`) flagged the ransomware binary, scheduled task, and malicious driver service, forensic analysis of `/disk` revealed additional **silent persistence** (Registry Run key) and **silent defense evasion** (Security log clearing) that bypassed initial automated detections.\n\n---\n\n## Attack Chain Analysis\n\n### Step 1: External Credential Access & Lateral Movement\n- **Techniques**: MITRE ATT&CK T1110 (Brute Force) & T1021.001 (Remote Desktop Protocol)\n- **Evidence & Findings**: The attacker targeted the exposed RDP interface on host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). Because NLA was disabled (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`), the attacker performed password brute-forcing from origin IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) and obtained interactive access.\n\n### Step 2: Execution & Payload Dropping\n- **Techniques**: MITRE ATT&CK T1059.001 (PowerShell Execution) & T1486 (Data Encrypted for Impact)\n- **Evidence & Findings**: Upon gaining access, the attacker dropped and executed a ransomware binary at `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` (`/sas/alerts.json:3`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`). The ransomware sample encrypts user files with a `.locked` extension and drops a ransom note. Strings in the binary revealed embedded Monero mining/ransomware telemetry including pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.rdp.evil:3333` and wallet `4A0000000000000000000e4435cc95c5` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`).\n  - SHA-256 (`svc.exe`): `4f8a5c4380a18bca293c7e9130caf957973cc733e9b2c32c2e5240aa9e2c2dae` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`)\n\n### Step 3: Persistence Establishment\n1. **Scheduled Task Persistence (Alerted)**:\n   - **Technique**: MITRE ATT&CK T1053.005 (Scheduled Task)\n   - **Evidence**: Scheduled task `UpdateHelper` configured via `schtasks` to execute `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` every 5 minutes (`/sas/alerts.json:11`, `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`).\n   - SHA-256 (`UpdateHelper`): `2c2313138723024ae31eb2d8c399cc3f47ffd7221937f098247629dba83d730d` (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`)\n\n2. **Malicious Service Persistence (Alerted)**:\n   - **Technique**: MITRE ATT&CK T1543.003 (Windows Service)\n   - **Evidence**: Malicious Windows service `svc-helper` registered to load driver file `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` at system boot (`/sas/alerts.json:19`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`). Strings confirm helper service capability linked to Monero wallet `4A0000000000000000000e4435cc95c5` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`).\n   - SHA-256 (`svc-helper.sys`): `8525c122105c20ecbf866f40d8d60ad1fbbe21fd07a6b77c79182631931ede86` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`)\n\n3. **Registry Run Key Persistence (SILENT / UNALERTED)**:\n   - **Technique**: MITRE ATT&CK T1547.001 (Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder)\n   - **Evidence**: Examination of the SOFTWARE registry hive (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) revealed an unalerted Run key value `svc` set to auto-execute `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` upon user logon. This finding was omitted from the automated alert feed (`/sas/alerts.json:1`) and was uncovered via forensic disk analysis (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).\n   - SHA-256 (`SOFTWARE`): `b08f4418b698c040964ae535a0ed3ea9c7b2ca83ffb0d32bd5c536c63e3c4971` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`)\n\n### Step 4: Defense Evasion & Anti-Forensics (SILENT / UNALERTED)\n- **Technique**: MITRE ATT&CK T1070.001 (Clear Windows Event Logs)\n- **Evidence**: The attacker cleared the Security event log (`EventID 1102`) to erase records of interactive logons and process creations (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`). This anti-forensic action was silent in the primary alert feed (`/sas/alerts.json:1`).\n- **Recovery**: Residual forensic evidence recovered from backup security registry hive `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` and system log `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` confirmed C2 beaconing activity to `198.51.100.92` (`update-rdp.example.cn`) and Administrator credential cache access (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`).\n\n---\n\n## Observed Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)\n\n| Indicator Type | Value | Evidence Citation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Source IP / C2 IP | `198.51.100.92` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` |\n| C2 Domain | `update-rdp.example.cn` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` |\n| Mining Pool | `stratum+tcp://xmr.rdp.evil:3333` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:7`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` |\n| Monero Wallet | `4A0000000000000000000e4435cc95c5` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` |\n| Ransomware Binary | `/Users/Public/svc.exe` | `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json:3` |\n| Scheduled Task | `UpdateHelper` | `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`, `/sas/alerts.json:11` |\n| Driver Service | `svc-helper` (`/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`) | `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`, `/sas/alerts.json:19` |\n| Registry Run Key | `HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\\svc` | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` |\n| Cleared Log Event | Security EventID 1102 | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx` |\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
