ics Event ID 1102 log clearing observed. Backup cleared log for offsite forensics and restore baseline logging. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` |\n| 7 | Quarantine exploit implant | `/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` | Proposed | Added containment item: DoublePulsar-class SMB exploit implant dropped in Temp folder. Backup and move to quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n| 8 | Quarantine LSASS dump & perform domain credential resets | `/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` | Proposed | Added credential recovery item: LSASS dump file captured by attacker. Quarantine file and force password resets for all active accounts on host. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n| 9 | Quarantine ransomware payload & isolate host | `/Users/Public/enc.exe` | Proposed | Added impact containment item: Ransomware binary dropped in Public directory. Isolate network interface and backup/quarantine binary. Citation: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Phase-by-Phase Execution Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Containment & Isolation\n1. **Network Containment:** Isolate host `smb-prod-01` from internal VLANs while retaining out-of-band management connectivity.\n2. **Firewall Rule Update:** Block inbound and outbound traffic to/from C2 IP `198.51.100.218` and domain `update-smb.example.cn`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`.\n3. **SMB Service Containment:** Stop the Server service (`net stop lanmanserver`) to immediately stop further SMBv1 exploitation.\n\n### Phase 2: Preservative Quarantine & Eradication\n1. **File Quarantine (Not Direct Deletion):** Create encrypted quarantine directory (`C:\\Quarantine\\SOC-2026-0811\\`) and move malicious binaries/dumps:\n   - Move `/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`.\n   - Move `/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`.\n   - Move `/Users/Public/enc.exe` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`.\n   - Move `/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` -> Quarantine. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.\n2. **WMI Persistence Removal:** Backup WMI repository (`/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`) to quarantine, then execute `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\\subscription | Remove-CimInstance` to purge unauthorized `__EventFilter` and `CommandLineEventConsumer` instances. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`.\n3. **Vulnerability Eradication:** Disable SMBv1 feature (`Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol -NoRestart`) and apply security update MS17-010 / KB4012212 to update `/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`.\n4. **Credential Revocation:** Perform mandatory password reset for local Administrator, Domain accounts, and service accounts logged onto `smb-prod-01`. Revoke cached Kerberos tickets / NTLM hashes. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`.\n\n### Phase 3: Recovery & Verification\n1. **System Restoration:** Reboot system into safe mode, verify `srv.sys` is updated, ensure `wbemcomn.dll` in `wbem` directory is removed, and confirm no rogue WMI consumers exist.\n2. **SIEM & Logging Verification:** Verify central logging via Winlogbeat/Syslog is capturing active events from `/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`. Citation: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`.\n3. **Network Verification:** Run vulnerability scan against host `smb-prod-01` on port 445/tcp to confirm SMBv1 is disabled and MS17-010 is resolved. Citation: `/sas/vulns.json`.\n4. **Re-integration:** Re-connect network interface to production network under monitoring for 72 hours.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
