e-forcing (`T1110`) resulting from Network Level Authentication (NLA) being disabled (`UserAuthentication = 0`).\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion & Confidence Level\n- **Vulnerability-Driven Access**: Explicitly Absent.\n- **Confidence**: HIGH (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:3`, `/sas/vulns.json:1`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).\n- **Remediation Focus**: Shift resources away from non-applicable software patching (e.g. BlueKeep) toward credential hygiene, RDP exposure restriction, and enforcing Network Level Authentication.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
