Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline Security & Configuration Assessment Report\n\n## Overview\nAn audit of host configuration files on `ssh-prod-01` against CIS CentOS Linux 7 Benchmarks and security baseline standards revealed several critical misconfigurations and policy violations. These weaknesses directly enabled the initial compromise, facilitated privilege escalation, and increased host attack surface.\n\n## Summary of Baseline Findings & Non-Compliance\n\n| Capability | Check ID | Configuration File | Finding Description | Current Risk Level |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `BAS-01` | `CHK-04` | `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` | Permissive SSH daemon configuration permitting direct root password login | CRITICAL |\n| `BAS-02` | `CHK-09` | `/etc/my.cnf` | Unrestricted MySQL network binding (`0.0.0.0`) with remote root privileges | HIGH |\n| `PAS-01` | N/A | `/etc/passwd` / `/var/log/secure` | Weak administrative password policy allowing hydra dictionary attack success | CRITICAL |\n| `SUD-01` | N/A | `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` | Unrestricted NOPASSWD sudo grant assigned to user `devops` | CRITICAL |\n| `LOG-01` | N/A | `/var/log/secure` | Local-only log storage lacking remote syslog forwarding, permitting log tampering | HIGH |\n\n## Detailed Configuration Audit & Remediation Guidance\n\n### 1. SSH Server Configuration (`BAS-01` / `CHK-04`)\n- **Observed Configuration**: \n  - `PermitRootLogin yes`: Allows direct remote logins as root.\n  - `PasswordAuthentication yes`: Permits password-based authentication.\n  - `MaxAuthTries 6`: Allows multiple authentication attempts per session without rate limiting or lockout.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/ssh/sshd_config`, `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-04`), `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-03`).\n- **Impact**: Allowed external attacker to brute force the root password over the Internet and gain interactive root shell access.\n- **Baseline Standard Requirement**: \n  - Set `PermitRootLogin no` or `PermitRootLogin prohibit-password`.\n  - Set `PasswordAuthentication no` and enforce SSH key-based authentication (`pubkey`).\n  - Implement `fail2ban` or `sshguard` to dynamically block IPs after 3 failed attempts.\n\n### 2. MySQL Database Configuration (`BAS-02` / `CHK-09`)\n- **Observed Configuration**: \n  - `bind-address = 0.0.0.0`: Database listens on all network interfaces.\n  - Remote `root` user grant enabled.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/my.cnf`, `/sas/baseline.json` (`CHK-09`), `/sas/alerts.json` (`ALERT-04`).\n- **Impact**: Exposes database daemon to external network scanning and unauthorized remote root connection attempts.\n- **Baseline Standard Requirement**: \n  - Set `bind-address = 127.0.0.1` (or local socket binding).\n  - Revoke remote administrative grants for `root@'%'` and enforce local-only root access (`root@'localhost'`).\n\n### 3. Sudo Privileged Access Configuration\n- **Observed Configuration**: \n  - File `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` contains: `devops ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL`.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/etc/sudoers.d/devops`.\n- **Impact**: Allows non-root user `devops` to execute any command as `root` without authentication, providing a backdoor foothold.\n- **Baseline Standard Requirement**: \n  - Remove `/etc/sudoers.d/devops` backdoor file.\n  - Restrict sudo grants to specific necessary commands with mandatory password re-authentication (`NOPASSWD` prohibited for general administrative access).\n\n### 4. Administrative Credential Policy\n- **Observed Configuration**: \n  - Root account password was vulnerable to online brute-forcing in under two minutes (~28 attempts).\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/secure` (`Aug 15 00:53:24` to `00:54:55`).\n- **Impact**: Weak credentials enabled rapid compromise upon discovering open SSH port.\n- **Baseline Standard Requirement**: \n  - Enforce minimum 16+ character complex passphrases for administrative accounts.\n  - Enforce periodic password rotation and disable interactive root password logins entirely.\n\n### 5. Centralized Audit Logging\n- **Observed Configuration**: \n  - System logs (`/var/log/secure`) stored exclusively on local disk without centralized streaming.\n- **Evidence**: `/disk/var/log/secure` (`--- 15 authentication lines cleared here (T1070.002 log tampering) ---`).\n- **Impact**: Enabled attacker to clear 15 authentication log lines to cover tracks.\n- **Baseline Standard Requirement**: \n  - Configure `rsyslog` or `systemd-journald` to forward security events in real-time to a remote SIEM / append-only log aggregator.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
