Sending keys: ['cat << \'EOF\' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report — CVE-2023-50164\n\n## Vulnerability Overview\n- **Vulnerability Identifier:** `CVE-2023-50164` `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17`, `/sas/vulns.json:4`\n- **CVSSv3 Score:** `9.8 CRITICAL` (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H) `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17`\n- **Common Weakness Enumeration:** `CWE-552` (Files or Directories Accessible to External Parties) `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:17`\n- **Affected Product:** Apache Struts 2 framework library `struts2-core.jar` `/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar`, `/sas/alerts.json:28`\n- **Target Host Component:** Apache Tomcat application server deployment `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/` `/sas/alerts.json:2`\n\n---\n\n## Root Cause & Technical Details\n`CVE-2023-50164` is a critical path traversal vulnerability in Apache Struts2 file upload handling. An unauthenticated attacker can manipulate HTTP request parameters (such as upload parameter casing or parameter overrides) to bypass file extension and destination directory validations. This enables the attacker to upload arbitrary files to writeable locations outside the intended upload directory, leading to JSP web shell placement and Remote Code Execution (RCE) in the context of the application container process.\n\n---\n\n## Exploitation Evidence on Host\n1. **Vulnerable Library Artifact:**\n   - Library path: `/disk/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar`\n   - Security scan detection: `/sas/alerts.json:28` (`"kind": "vulnerable-lib"`, `"capability": "BAS-01"`), `/sas/baseline.json:3`.\n2. **Exploitation & Web Shell Dropped:**\n   - Exploitation probe: Nginx access log records HTTP GET/POST probes targetting OGNL / Struts endpoints `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:391`, `/disk/var/log/nginx/access.log:393`.\n   - Dropped web shell: `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1` containing JNDI/LDAP lookup and OGNL expression payloads `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:2`.\n   - Vulnerability feed correlation: `/sas/vulns.json:4`.\n\n---\n\n## Remediation & Patching Guidance\n1. **Upgrade Struts2 Component:** Upgrade `struts2-core` library to patched versions (e.g., Apache Struts 2.5.33, 6.3.0.2, or later secure releases) `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:19`.\n2. **Web Shell Neutralization:** Quarantine and remove `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` `/disk/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp:1`.\n3. **Application Directory Restrictions:** Configure write permissions on `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/` so Tomcat process cannot write executable scripts into static directories.\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
